  "name": "Learning from Others, Acting for You: Cross-User Memory Sharing for LLM Agents",
  "notes": "Main Mind2Web evaluation uses 252 recorded tasks assigned to 20 simulated users, frozen demonstration-derived memory and task-macro step metrics; it is not a live-browser completion test. The main split withholds same-site local experience, and sharing gains shrink when local coverage rises. Mind2Web has no preference channel; preference claims come from separate service and coding settings. User-bound retrieval is not a demonstrated privacy or security guarantee. Selected sections were source-read; no independent reproduction.",
  "published_at": "2026-09-26",
  "relations": [],
  "review_status": "curated",
  "scope": "core",
  "summary": "ShareMem consolidates reusable experience across users while keeping preference retrieval user-bound; its web evaluation predicts target elements and actions on recorded Mind2Web states.",
